    "body": "Fixes #299.\n\nDiscard the cached source iterator when restoring or resetting an `EpochizeDataset`, so subsequent iteration starts from restored child state. Uninterrupted virtual epochs still reuse their iterator. Saved fields and checkpoint format are unchanged.\n\n## Review changes\n\nThe regression now extends the existing crude-dataset checkpoint test. The original packed two-worker case still reconstructs a loader before restoration, as required by the active-worker API. The added zero-worker case explicitly enables virtual epochs, advances a live loader, restores its checkpoint in place, and compares all 100 resumed batch keys exactly. With the unchanged EpochizeDataset, that new case fails; restoring the patch passes both cases.\n\nThe prior revision had used the forbidden active-worker restoration path and omitted virtual epochs. Those test errors are corrected without weakening the loader guard or modifying packing buffers. No standalone synthetic dataset test is retained.\n\nThe use case is demonstrated with the repository's local end-to-end fixtures. This does not claim an observed production training incident.\n\n## Current validation\n\nRefreshed on 15 October 2026 onto `develop` at `bcfd8f5`. Head `76f07e7` preserves the checkpoint regression and uses the renamed upstream `recipe_path` fixture.\n\n`python -m pytest -q tests/test_crudedataset.py tests/test_file_cache_pool.py tests/test_sample_utils.py`: **20 passed, 2 subtests passed** on macOS CPU/Python 3.12.14. The tests use real local files, loader workers, media decoding and the local S3 emulator. Full repository Ruff, changed-file Ruff formatting and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nTest sources and logs are on the contribution drive; transient fixtures use native temporary storage for Unix IPC support. Optional boto3 and PyAV dependencies were installed separately for validation; no project dependency or workflow changed. Existing platform and deprecation warnings remain. GPU, distributed multi-rank and the full repository suite were not run. Upstream workflows require maintainer approval.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
