    {
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "Thanks @voegtlel — I folded this into the existing crude-dataset save/restore e2e test and removed the standalone synthetic dataset test. The e2e now restores the checkpoint onto the already-used loader after further iteration, which is the case that leaves EpochizeDataset holding a stale active source iterator without this fix. The use case is checkpoint/resume in a larger multimodal PyTorch/Megatron/NeMo training pipeline, where a long-running loader is restored in place after partial iteration rather than reconstructed from scratch. Ready for re-review.",
